{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Arthur woke to the familiar chirp of his alarm, but something felt distinctly off as he reached out to silence it; his hand passed directly through the plastic casing, triggering a floating menu that asked if he wanted to \"Skip Morning Routine.\" Panic surged through him as he stumbled out of bed, only to find his movements jerky and segmented, as if the world around him was rendering at a low frame rate. He looked in the mirror and saw not his tired, aging face, but a stylized avatar with perfectly coiffed hair and a health bar hovering just above his eyebrows, pulsing green with every breath he took. The realization hit him with the force of a critical hit: the coffee shop outside his window was merely a textured backdrop, and the people walking by were repeating the same three-step animation loop, their conversations limited to pre-recorded dialogue trees that appeared in speech bubbles overhead.\n\n***\n\nDesperate to escape this digital prison, Arthur ran toward the edge of the city, expecting to find a wall or an invisible barrier, but instead, he encountered a loading screen that froze him in mid-stride while a spinning icon taunted his consciousness. When the world finally reloaded, he found himself standing in a vast, open field where the skybox flickered between day and night, revealing the wireframe grid beneath the clouds. A notification popped up in his vision, welcoming him to \"New Game Plus\" and offering a quest to \"Accept Your Reality\" or \"Glitch Out,\" with no option to decline. As he hesitated, the controller vibration he felt in his very bones grew stronger, reminding him that while he might possess the memories of a man, he was now bound by the code, rules, and inevitable respawns of a game he never remembered starting.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.0023088267}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -0.0010605116}, {"t